# Intent: The games page and the Apps and Games walls at finger size (owner review 2026-11-18, the physical standard in docs/design/screen-style.md; batch UX13e). The games page is a scrolling grid of two columns of 148 by 64 px tiles with 8 px gaps and an 8 px margin, as many rows as there are games (13 today), with an always-on scroll bar instead of the More tile and its paging; a tile is the name in the 20 px body text over its best score in 16 px, a long name ("Rock Paper Scissors") wraps in 16 px and keeps its best line, and the lines are stacked and centered in the tile so they cannot overlap in any language. The More screen's own games list keeps the old paging helpers (patch UX13b changes that screen). The Apps and Games walls keep their picture tiles but take the 8 px gap and 6 px margin (150 by 86 tiles). Display only: no safety, lock, cue, limiter or head-motion code.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages_core.h, maipai_apps_core.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: Games shows two rows of tiles, each name and its best score on clean lines, a scroll bar on the right; a swipe up shows the next games down to the last; tapping a tile starts that game; the Apps and Games walls have an even gap between the tiles.
# Kconfig: none

